       arrives (NATS healthy), S3* findings never do. The nucleus CAN publish; S3* CANNOT.
       Findings are written to events.jsonl (107) only."
    prime_hypothesis:
      "async-nats publish() QUEUES only; sent on the connection's flush.
       short-lived connection ∧ drop before flush ⟹ message LOST SILENTLY
       (publish() returned Ok, nothing sent). DS's guess was exactly this.
       check whether S3*'s algedonic publish:
         (a) reuses a persistent connection or opens ad-hoc per finding,
         (b) awaits flush()/drain before the connection drops,
         (c) uses the canonical helper (vsf_agent::nats::connect) or an ad-hoc connect,
         (d) publishes to the subject the ledger actually subscribes to."
    fix_principle:
      "persistent connection via the canonical helper ∧ explicit flush/drain
       before ∀ drop. ad-hoc-per-finding ⟹ await flush() before scope exit"
    escalate_to_opus:
      "IF the divergence is in async-nats internals (flush semantics, connection lifecycle,
