  // ─── 5.3 MERKLE-F64-FIX (HIGH, 2026-07-17) — false content_tamper from f64 round-trip ───
  MERKLE_F64_FIX = {
    id: "MERKLE-F64-FIX"
    owner: "DS [S] impl+validation  ·  Claude [O] review"
    date: "2026-07-17"
    severity: "HIGH"
    status: "DESIGN"
    depends: "LEDGER-DEAF-P3 Leg B done"
    problem:
      "After Leg B (raw line via NATS), S3* continues raising false content_tamper (merkle
       _break sev 10) in ~44% of events. ROOT CAUSE (DS found, [O] confirmed with exact
       arithmetic): canonical_hash commits f64 BIT PATTERNS. The WRITER (nucleus) hashes
       its in-memory f64 bits (e.g. 0x3fefffffe0153e60). The VERIFIER (S3*) reads the
       decimal string ('0.9999999405499231') and RE-PARSES to f64 via serde_json → which
       (measured) gives 0x3fefffffe0153e61, 1 ULP more — and recomputes a divergent hash →
       FALSE content_tamper. Python (correctly rounded parser) gives ...60 and matches;
       the chain is genuinely intact (verify_chain_diverse.py 2000/2000 clean)."
    fix_principle:
      "The verifier must recompute the hash over the SAME f64 bits the writer committed.
       writer serializes losslessly (ryu shortest round-trip); verifier recovers
       the exact bits via a correctly-rounded parser, ¬serde_json's fast-path.
       ∄ format change ▪ ∄ change to WHAT is hashed (still f64 bits)
       ▪ only HOW the verifier recovers"
    avenue_B_preferred:
      "B (preferred, scoped to S3*): in vsf-s3-star's detect_content_tamper path, get the
       original decimal string and re-parse floats with stdlib f64::from_str before hashing.
       Localized to vsf-s3-star → deploy S3* only (LXC 107), nucleus intact. Smaller blast
       radius."
    avenue_A_fallback:
      "A (fallback, shared crate): enable serde_json/arbitrary_precision in vsf_agent so
       Number keeps its string. Simpler code but WORKSPACE-WIDE (feature unification) →
       the nucleus recompiles too → gates 2+3 become mandatory. Use ONLY if B infeasible,
       STOP for [O] review before touching the nucleus."
    avenue_C_last_resort:
      "C (last resort, format v3): redefine canonical_hash to commit the canonical
       serialized BYTES rather than f64 bits. Structural kills all fragility but touches
       the KERNEL + chain format + self-reference. Only if A and B fail."
    validation_gates:
      "1. fix works: S3* recomputed hash == stored, on the ~88/200 mismatching
       2. writer intact: canonical_hash pinned test passes
       3. (⟸ nucleus recompiles, avenue A) chain byte-identical pre/post
       4. audit ¬weakened (negative control): an altered f64 event STILL flags
          content_tamper ⟹ ∄ false-negative regression"
    interim_mitigation:
      "DO NOTHING interim. False rate ~2-3/hour (modest, not a flood), sev 10 but the chain
       is PROVEN intact. Re-suppressing S3* reintroduces the deaf-ledger blind spot
       (detector_liveness). Keep S3* ALIVE; land the real fix."
    resolution_state: "LANDED, by a THIRD path neither avenue describes
      (claude_review 2026-08-07): serde_json pinned =1.0.150 with feature
      `float_roundtrip` in BOTH vsf-nucleus/Cargo.toml:30 ∧ vsf-s3-star/Cargo.toml:17.
      ¬avenue B (stdlib f64::from_str in S3*) ∧ ¬avenue A (arbitrary_precision).
      float_roundtrip makes serde_json's own parser correctly-rounded ⟹ writer ∧ verifier
      recover the SAME bits, workspace-wide, without touching detect_content_tamper.
      The avenues above are kept as the DESIGN RECORD; they are ¬what shipped."
  }

  // ─── 5.4 SEMANTIC-DIVERGENCE-RCA (MEDIUM, 2026-07-18) ───
  SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE_RCA = {
    id: "SEMANTIC-DIVERGENCE-RCA"
    owner: "Claude [O]  ·  DS [S] diagnosis (read-only)"
    date: "2026-07-18"
    severity: "MEDIUM"
    status: "DIAGNOSE"
    depends: "MERKLE-F64-FIX done (killed merkle_break; semantic_divergence is the residual noise)"
    problem:
      "S3* emits semantic_divergence (sev 7.0 — the spec's 8.0 was wrong, resolved §1) ~1
       per audit cycle, dominant ledger family after killing merkle_break (273 entries,
       still growing). All audit_target=shadow_recompute."
    observed_data:
      "SYSTEMATIC PATTERN (not random):
         claimed (nucleus)  = 1.000000 EXACT, always
         recomputed (S3*)   = ~0.979 (0.9788–0.9798), varies little
         diff               = ~0.021, ALWAYS just above ε=0.02
       Examples: 0.979127/1.0/0.020873 · 0.978823/1.0/0.021177 · 0.979782/1.0/0.020218.
       EXACT 1.0 (a real cosine is almost never exact) + consistent offset REFUTE the
       buffer-gap hypothesis (which would give random diffs)."
    leading_hypothesis:
      "SEMANTIC CONTRACT MISMATCH. The stasis_cos=1.0 the nucleus sends in invariant_check
       is probably a FLAG 'all invariants pass = OK', not a literal cosine. S3*/shadow
       _recompute treats it as literal, recomputes the real cosine (~0.979), and flags the
       diff. Comparing a FLAG against a MEASUREMENT → false positive. System is HEALTHY:
       real stasis_cos ~0.979 is well above the viability threshold (0.70)."
    alternatives:
      ["B (nucleus truly clamps): nucleus SHOULD report the literal cosine and clamps to
        1.0 → S3* is right, a nucleus REPORTING bug (integrity).",
       "C (S3* recompute wrong): both are the literal cosine but S3* computes differently
        (normalization, missing dims, stale state) → S3* recompute bug."]
    verdict_protocol:
      "1. NUCLEUS: where is invariant_check emitted, what's in stasis_cos — literal cosine
       similarity OR a flag (1.0 = invariants OK)?
       2. S3*/shadow_recompute: what's extracted as `claimed`, how is `recomputed` computed?
       3. VERDICT: do claimed and recomputed refer to the SAME magnitude?
          · DIFFERENT (flag vs measurement) → leading hypothesis (contract) CONFIRMED.
          · SAME, nucleus=1.0 clamped → alternative B (nucleus bug).
          · SAME, S3* miscomputes → alternative C (S3* bug)."
    design_smell:
      "∀ verdict: a SEMANTIC FLAG in a NUMERIC field (stasis_cos) is a smell —
       confuses measurement with state. separate flag from measurement
       (model ≡ reality: each field means ONE thing)"
    resolution_state: "diagnosis owner=DS (read-only + report); fix design by Claude after verdict."
  }

  // ─── 5.5 SEMANTIC-DIVERGENCE-FIX (MEDIUM, 2026-07-18) ───
  SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE_FIX = {
    id: "SEMANTIC-DIVERGENCE-FIX"
    owner: "DS [S] impl  ·  Claude [O] review + nucleus deploy"
    date: "2026-07-18"
    severity: "MEDIUM"
    status: "DESIGN"
    depends: "SEMANTIC-DIVERGENCE-RCA verdict — [O] approved direction C over A"
    diagnosis_source: "@dir_rca q4-semantic-divergence-rca.md (DS), confirmed by [O] reading
                       operational.rs L747/L761/L1234."
    root_cause:
      "operational.rs: stepper.step() computes stasis_cos on the PRE-ingest state (L747);
       ingest overwrites Block B (L761); the snapshot for S3* (shadow_sv, L1234) is captured
       POST-ingest. The event ships a stasis_cos and a state_vector from DIFFERENT PHASES
       of the tick → S3* cannot reproduce the value → false semantic_divergence (~0.02)
       every cycle. The stasis_cos audit is de-facto broken (always diverges)."
    decision:
      "OPTION C (move the capture), NOT option A (raise ε to 0.03). A does NOT fix — it
       SILENCES: blinds the stasis_cos audit at 0-0.03 (a real divergence there would be
       invisible) and is fragile (observed max 0.026 → margin 0.004; worse under load).
       C RESTORES the audit. Same principle as the whole saga (merkle/f64/wail): repair,
       don't silence."
    fix:
      "Move the capture block shadow_sv/shadow_st (L1233-1239) to immediately AFTER
       stepper.step() (L747-748), BEFORE ingest (758), coupling (767), ethics (769+), and
       LIFECYCLE (1219). So shadow_sv = the EXACT state stasis_cos was computed on. Keep
       the condition (tick % SHADOW_SAMPLE_K == 0 && stasis.n_observations() > 0). Do NOT
       touch the dynamics. Do NOT touch ε."
    principle: "An audit ships the VALUE and the DATUM it derived from as a CONSISTENT PAIR."
    gates:
      "1. build --release in LXC 108.
       2. CRITICAL — spec_boot: dynamics IDENTICAL to baseline (viable_full=true,
          governed=true, cycles>0, mean_dL<0). The capture is read-only; should move
          nothing. If it changed → STOP.
       3. R4 deploy to LXC 101 (nucleus — care).
       4. Verify: S3* recompute matches stasis_cos (diff→~0); ZERO new semantic_divergence
          post-deploy.
       5. ε stays 0.02 (do NOT touch alert_predicate — we fix the SOURCE, not the tolerance)."
    companion:
      "APART, ¬in this fix (keep the nucleus diff MINIMUM): raise display
       precision in misleading logs ({:.6} → {:.9}). cosmetic; batch later.
       storage is already full-fidelity — rounding is per-consumer, ¬at source"
    resolution_state: "APPLIED ∧ VERIFIED (claude_review 2026-08-07): operational.rs:763
      captures (shadow_sv, shadow_st) BEFORE coupling (:780), and the code carries the
      invariant in its own comment at :760 — 'Must happen BEFORE ingest overwrites'.
      Option C landed as designed."
  }

